6. COMPILER GRAMMAR AND SUPPORTED C SUBSET
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Grammar Overview (EBNF-style):
  Program         ::= TopLevelDecl* EOF
  TopLevelDecl    ::= FunctionDef | Statement
  FunctionDef     ::= "int" IDENTIFIER "(" ParameterList? ")" Block
  ParameterList   ::= "int" IDENTIFIER ("," "int" IDENTIFIER)*
  Statement       ::= VarDecl | ArrayDecl | Block | ForLoop | WhileLoop
                    | IfStmt | ReturnStmt | PrintStmt | ExprStmt | AssignmentStmt
  VarDecl         ::= "int" IDENTIFIER ("=" Expr)? ";"
  ArrayDecl       ::= "int" IDENTIFIER "[" INT_LITERAL "]" ("=" "{" ExprList? "}")? ";"
  Block           ::= "{" Statement* "}"
  ForLoop         ::= "for" "(" ForInit? ";" Expr? ";" ForUpdate? ")" Statement
  WhileLoop       ::= "while" "(" Expr ")" Statement
  IfStmt          ::= "if" "(" Expr ")" Statement ("else" Statement)?
  ReturnStmt      ::= "return" Expr? ";"
  PrintStmt       ::= "print" "(" Expr ")" ";"
  AssignmentStmt  ::= (IDENTIFIER | ArrayAccess) ("=" | "+=" | "-=" | "*=" | "/=") Expr ";"
  Expr            ::= LogicalOrExpr
  LogicalOrExpr   ::= LogicalAndExpr ("||" LogicalAndExpr)*
  LogicalAndExpr  ::= EqualityExpr ("&&" EqualityExpr)*
  EqualityExpr    ::= RelationalExpr (("==" | "!=") RelationalExpr)*
  RelationalExpr  ::= AdditiveExpr (("<" | "<=" | ">" | ">=") AdditiveExpr)*
  AdditiveExpr    ::= MultiplicativeExpr (("+" | "-") MultiplicativeExpr)*
  Multiplicative  ::= UnaryExpr (("*" | "/" | "%") UnaryExpr)*
  UnaryExpr       ::= ("-" | "!" | "++" | "--") UnaryExpr | PrimaryExpr
  PrimaryExpr     ::= INT_LITERAL | IDENTIFIER | ArrayAccess | "(" Expr ")"
  ArrayAccess     ::= IDENTIFIER "[" Expr "]"


7. TOKEN AND AST REPRESENTATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Token:
  {
    "type": "INT" | "IDENTIFIER" | "INT_LITERAL" | "ASSIGN" | ... ,
    "value": "arr" | 42 | "+=" | ... ,
    "line": int,
    "column": int
  }

AST Nodes (all serialize via to_dict()):
  - Program: body: [ASTNode]
  - FunctionDef: name, return_type, params, body
  - VarDecl: type_name, name, initializer
  - ArrayDecl: type_name, name, size, initializers: [ASTNode]
  - Block: statements: [ASTNode]
  - Assignment: target, value
  - CompoundAssignment: target, op, value
  - ForLoop: init, condition, update, body
  - WhileLoop: condition, body
  - IfStatement: condition, then_branch, else_branch
  - ReturnStatement: value
  - PrintStatement: expression
  - BinaryOp: left, op, right
  - UnaryOp: op, operand, is_prefix
  - ArrayAccess: array_name, index
  - Identifier: name
  - IntLiteral: value


8. SEMANTIC-ANALYSIS RULES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Variables and arrays must be declared before use.
2. Identifiers cannot be re-declared in the same lexical scope level.
3. Scalar variables cannot be indexed like arrays.
4. Array initializer list element count must not exceed declared array capacity.
5. Array size must be a strictly positive integer constant (> 0).
6. Constant integer division by zero generates a semantic diagnostic.
7. Static array bounds check is enforced when index expression is a constant literal.


